    "text": "Open Accounting, then Budgets, and select Draft next year’s budget.\nIf the page says next year \"isn't open in the books yet\", an HOA admin selects Open next fiscal year, then confirms. You can also do this from Accounting, then Fiscal periods. Your current year stays the current year until next year starts, so dues, bills and recurring entries keep posting where they do today. Board members see who to ask instead.\nCheck the Fund and the Budget year. The page shows which budget it started from and the dates of the actuals it used.\nSet the Inflation adjustment. It's 3% unless you change it, and it applies to every line.\nRead each line. Under the account name is the reason for its suggestion, for example \"Last year budget $24,000, actual $26,100, +3%\". Type a different amount wherever the board wants one. To go back to the suggestion, select Use suggestion.\nOptional: under Main changes vs last year, select Write a summary with AI for a short paragraph to put in the board packet.\nSelect Save as draft budget, check the totals, then select Save draft.",
